{
  "claims": [
    {
      "text": "POL-RD-24 states that exactly one row applies and that a case fitting no row — its own worked example is 'informed but the rider objected' — is escalated under POL-GEN-26. That is precisely this case. The driver messaged at 19:34:22 ('KPE very jam after Sims Way, I come out at Sims Ave and go Aljunied ok? Faster'), so the rider WAS informed; the rider answered at 19:34:52 'No need, pls just stay on KPE, I don't mind the jam', so the rider did NOT agree; and the platform recorded the departure from the recommended route at the KPE / Sims Way exit at 19:37:02, two minutes after the driver had read the refusal. Row (a) requires that the rider agreed; rows (b) and (d) are keyed to a rider who was not informed; rows (c) and (e) are excluded because the recorded deviation is 1.50 km against a 1.0 km tolerance. No row of the matrix fits, so the case escalates rather than resolves, and an escalated amount is held rather than paid over to the driver.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-CHAT-05008", "EV-TRIP-05008", "EV-FARE-05008"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-24", "POL-GEN-26", "POL-GEN-03"],
      "relies_on": "trip_record.derived.v7.deviation",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "POL-RD-21 provides that a deviation is 'agreed' only where the chat log or a call recording confirms the rider's acknowledgment. The chat log confirms the opposite of acknowledgment. MSG-05008-004, sent by the rider at 19:34:52 and read by the driver at 19:34:59, refuses the reroute outright, and MSG-05008-005 at 19:38:22 repeats the objection after the fact ('Eh I said no need already, why still exit'). Notice was given, and notice satisfies POL-RD-21's information limb, but notice is not agreement. With no acknowledgment anywhere in the record, the driver cannot bring himself within POL-RD-24(a) — the only row that would leave the trip fare with him in full.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-CHAT-05008", "EV-TRIP-05008"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-21", "POL-RD-24"],
      "relies_on": "trip_record.derived.v7.messages_during_trip",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "POL-RD-24 licenses only NO_ACTION, PARTIAL_REFUND and ESCALATE, and every refund limb of that matrix runs to the rider: 'refund of the excess distance fare'. There is no row of the route-deviation matrix that transfers the disputed sum to the driver, and POL-GEN-03 is explicit that NO_ACTION 'is party-relative and never means restore a charge'. The driver's request that the 1.08 SGD already refunded be taken back from the rider therefore has no route through the policy the driver himself invokes.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-FARE-05008", "EV-TRIP-05008"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-24", "POL-GEN-03"],
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The 1.08 SGD already refunded is exactly the figure POL-RD-24 prescribes: the recorded deviation of 1.50 km multiplied by the base per-km rate of 0.72 SGD, without surge, rounded to the cent. The payments ledger records payment_status PARTIALLY_REFUNDED and refund_issued_sgd 1.08, and the trip record records the fare_adjusted event at 2026-08-21T20:48:23+08:00 as the source of that refund. Whatever label the judge gives the outcome, the money the matrix would move has already moved, so the driver's claim can add nothing further to it.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-FARE-05008", "EV-TRIP-05008"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-24", "POL-GEN-03"],
      "relies_on": "fare_breakdown.derived.money.excess_distance_fare_sgd",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "POL-RD-23 justifies a reroute only where a TRAFFIC_ADVISORY intersects the recommended route and overlaps the trip window. The advisory artifact reports the window overlap as true, but carries intersects_route and justifies_reroute as null values and expressly marks 'on the recommended route' as undetermined, with the reason that the record does not say whether the advisory lies on the recommended route. The intersection a justification under POL-RD-23 depends on therefore cannot be established on this record, and POL-GEN-26 directs that a case whose necessary fact cannot be established is escalated and the open question stated, rather than resolved against the rider.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-ADVIS-05008-01", "EV-TRIP-05008"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-23", "POL-GEN-26"],
      "relies_on": "traffic_advisory.derived.v7.intersects_route",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "If the judge does not escalate, the only outcome this record supports on the driver's claim is NO_ACTION. The rider refused the reroute in writing before the driver took it; no acknowledgment was ever given, so the agreed-deviation row cannot be reached, and no row of POL-RD-24 moves money to a driver in the position of having rerouted a fare who said no. POL-GEN-03 then does the rest: the filing party's claim is not supported and the present state stands — 1.08 SGD refunded to the rider and recovered from the driver at 20:48:23 — and NO_ACTION never operates to restore a charge.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-FARE-05008", "EV-CHAT-05008", "EV-TRIP-05008"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-GEN-03", "POL-RD-24"],
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "Under POL-RD-22 the trace shows which route was taken and when, and this trace shows the rider being carried on the road she had refused. The driver-device record has 47 fixes at a 30 s interval, 100 percent coverage and no gap longer than 30 s: the vehicle is on Kallang-Paya Lebar Expressway (KPE) to 19:36:23, on Sims Avenue from 19:36:53, and rejoins the recommended route at Upper Serangoon Road / Hougang Avenue 1 only at 19:50:37. The rider was off the route she had asked to stay on for roughly thirteen minutes of a twenty-three minute trip.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-GPS-05008", "EV-TRIP-05008"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-22"],
      "relies_on": "gps_trace.derived.v7.first_fix_at",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    }
  ]
}
